The texts are the official constitutional text of the Republic of Benin, published openly by the Assemblée nationale du Bénin (assemblee-nationale.bj) and the Cour constitutionnelle du Bénin (courconstitutionnelle.bj). A constitution and other official legislative texts are public acts of the State; neither site states a reuse restriction on them. Credit the publishers as the source of the texts.

Laws, ordinances, decrees and orders (codes/, lois/, ordonnances/, decrets/, arretes/) are copied from the text layer
of the official PDFs published by the Secrétariat général du Gouvernement du Bénin (https://sgg.gouv.bj; no reuse
restriction stated) or, where that PDF is a scan or unreadable, from the copy of the national PDF in FAOLEX, the FAO
Legal Database (https://faolex.fao.org; FAO's terms allow reproduction for non-commercial purposes with acknowledgement
of FAO as the source). Official texts of a legislative, administrative or judicial nature are excluded from copyright
protection (Bangui Agreement, Annex VII, article 6). Each act's README.md and commit
trailers name the file it comes from.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
